      "slug": "empire-seam-dress-g285",
      "term": "Empire seam",
      "definition": "A horizontal join line worked directly under the bust. The bodice and skirt sections are worked separately and joined at this line. The skirt hangs as a straight column below, with no waist darts or side shaping to restrict the bump."
    },
    {
      "slug": "skirt-flare-g285",
      "term": "Skirt flare",
      "definition": "A gradual increase in stitch count added over the first 10 rows below the empire seam. Working one extra dc every 10 stitches for 10 rows adds gentle width at the hem without creating a fitted look. The flare keeps the fabric falling clear of the legs."
    }
  ],
